# Rust
target/

# Cargo.lock IS committed for this app (see Cargo's recommendation for
# binary/application crates). Without it, every CI run does a fresh
# dependency resolution against crates.io and any newly-published minor
# of e.g. `tauri = "^2"` can break the build with no code change on our
# side — that's how v0.0.17's first release attempt failed (tauri 2.11
# vs @tauri-apps/api 2.10 mismatch). Committing the lockfile pins both
# sides to the same versions across CI and dev.

# Tauri externalBin staging (populated by CI; never committed)
src-tauri/binaries/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
# Local artisan scripts are excluded by default. Build-essential scripts
# that produce committed artifacts (so future contributors can rebuild
# them) are listed as exceptions below. Note: `!` re-inclusion only
# works against `/scripts/*`, not `/scripts/` — git cannot re-include
# a file once its parent directory is excluded.
/scripts/*
!/scripts/generate-menu-icons.sh
!/scripts/regen-icons.sh
!/scripts/pre-push
!/scripts/install-hooks.sh
# Mints the TLS material for the remote surface. `remote::tls`'s
# fail-closed errors name this path as the remedy, and AGENTS.md
# documents it — an ignored script would point committed error messages
# at a file a fresh clone does not have.
!/scripts/mint-remote-cert.sh
# Local CI gate + its shared invariant checks. repo-invariants.sh is
# invoked by .github/workflows/ci.yml, so it MUST be committed.
!/scripts/preflight.sh
!/scripts/repo-invariants.sh
# Real-app layout check for Global → Config → Env Variables. Referenced by
# preflight.sh and by the `check:envvar-layout` package script, so leaving it
# out would point a committed gate at a file a fresh clone does not have.
!/scripts/check-envvar-layout.mjs
# Its unit tests, which vitest DOES run in CI (`scripts/**/*.test.mjs` is in
# vitest.config.ts's include). Leaving this ignored would put a test file in
# the working tree that no other clone has and CI never sees — the same
# never-ran-anywhere failure the web suite's hand-listed runner had.
!/scripts/check-envvar-layout.test.mjs
# Icon pipeline. `regen-icons.sh` was already excepted below; these two are
# the other half of it — the macOS 26 layered-icon compile step, and the
# structural checker both it and AGENTS.md tell you to run. A committed
# `Assets.car` that no one can rebuild is worse than no Assets.car.
!/scripts/build-macos-glass-icon.sh
!/scripts/verify-icons.py
# Locale-catalog gate. ci.yml runs it via `pnpm check:catalogs`, so the same
# rule as the entry above applies with teeth: leaving it out points a
# committed CI step at a file a fresh clone does not have, and the job fails
# on checkout rather than on a real finding.
!/scripts/check-catalogs.mjs
# Advisory scan for user-visible strings that never reached a catalog. Not a
# CI gate, but `pnpm scan:untranslated` is a committed package script and a
# script a fresh clone cannot run is worse than no script.
!/scripts/scan-untranslated.mjs
# Producer of assets/screenshots/ and web/public/screenshots/, both committed.
# `pnpm screenshots` runs it, and `cargo xtask verify-docs` fails when a
# SCREENSHOTS row there has no matching SHOTS row here — a two-file contract
# whose other half is committed. Same rule as the two entries above: nothing
# a committed file points at may be missing from a fresh clone.
!/scripts/capture-screenshots.mjs
# Producer of crates/claudepot-core/data/cc-env-spec.json, which the core
# crate embeds with include_str!. `cargo xtask verify-docs` re-runs it with
# --check, so an uncommitted producer would make that gate unrunnable.
!/scripts/build-cc-env-spec.py
dev-docs/

# Per-clone validator hosts for scripts/pre-push (internal hostnames —
# never committed; real values documented in CLAUDE.local.md).
.validator-hosts

# Claude Code local override files (read alongside CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md
# but kept out of version control). The general pattern catches any
# *.local.md file anywhere in the tree (the `*.local` pattern above
# only matches files literally ending in `.local`, not `.local.md`).
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.local.md
**/*.local.md

# Tauri's `pnpm tauri icon` command regenerates these on every run,
# but we don't ship for MSIX/iOS/Android, so any reappearance is dead
# bytes. Ignored so a stray `pnpm tauri icon` invocation doesn't
# stage them. The supported regen path is `scripts/regen-icons.sh`,
# which produces only the assets the bundler actually consumes.
src-tauri/icons/Square*Logo.png
src-tauri/icons/StoreLogo.png
src-tauri/icons/128x128@2x.png
src-tauri/icons/ios/
src-tauri/icons/android/

